/-!
# The reduction of Tag 0CBY to a base of finite type over the integers

The diagram of [Stacks, Tag 0CBY] is produced from the formal local structure of a split node by
[Stacks, Tag 0GDX], whose two standing hypotheses on the base `S` are that it is locally
Noetherian and that the local ring `𝒪_{S, s}` is a G-ring. Neither follows from the hypotheses of
Tag 0CBY, which place no condition on `S` at all: `Spec R[u, v]/(uv) ⟶ Spec R` is at-worst-nodal
of relative dimension one for every ring `R`, Noetherian or not. The first proof of Tag 0CBY
therefore opens by reducing to a base of finite type over the integers, where both hold — the
first because such a scheme is Noetherian, the second by [Stacks, Tag 07PX], a finite type
algebra over `ℤ` being a G-ring and its local rings being essentially of finite type over it.

This file carries out that reduction for `Stacks.NodalEtaleLocalStructure.StandardNodalDiagram`,
which is the form in which Tag 0GDX's conclusion is assembled by
`Stacks.NodalEtaleLocalStructure.standardNodalDiagramOfEtaleApproximation`. The reduction runs in
three steps: the assertion is local on source and target, so the base may be replaced by an
affine open and the source by an affine open above it; an affine scheme is the limit of the
spectra of the finitely generated `ℤ`-subalgebras of its coordinate ring; and the family descends
to a stage of that system, at-worst-nodal of relative dimension one and with the point still a
point of the relative singular subscheme, by [Stacks, Tags 01ZM, 0C5F and 0C3I].

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isGRing_stalk_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj` — **[Stacks, Tag 07PX] at a
  stage of the Noetherian approximation of an affine scheme**: the local rings of the spectrum of
  a finitely generated `ℤ`-subalgebra are G-rings.
* `Stacks.NodalEtaleLocalStructure.nonempty_standardNodalDiagram_of_isLimit` — the diagram
  descends along a cofiltered limit of quasi-compact quasi-separated schemes with affine
  transition morphisms.
* `Stacks.NodalEtaleLocalStructure.nonempty_standardNodalDiagram_of_finiteTypeOverInt` — **the
  reduction**: if the diagram of Tag 0CBY exists for every at-worst-nodal morphism of relative
  dimension one over an affine base of finite type over the integers, at every point of its
  relative singular subscheme, then it exists for every such morphism over an arbitrary base.
  Its hypothesis is discharged, and Tag 0CBY thereby proved, by
  `Stacks.NodalEtaleLocalStructure.nonempty_standardNodalDiagram_of_isAtWorstNodal` in
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.NodalEtaleLocalStructureAssembly`.

## Implementation notes

The limit step is the analogue of
`Stacks.NodalEtaleLocalStructure.nonempty_nodalChartNeighbourhood_of_isLimit` for the diagram
rather than the chart, and it is cheaper: the chart form's base change along the morphism from
the limit to a stage is stated only for affine bases, because the chart names an affine
neighbourhood of the image point, so the chart form's limit lemma must assume the limit and all
the stages affine. The diagram's base change,
`Stacks.NodalEtaleLocalStructure.nonempty_standardNodalDiagram_of_isPullback`, has no such
hypothesis, so only quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of the stages are required here —
exactly what [Stacks, Tags 01ZM and 0C5F] ask for.

The affine system used in the reduction is the elementary one,
`AlgebraicGeometry.specAdjoinFinsetDiagram`: the spectra of the subalgebras `ℤ[i]` generated by
the finite subsets `i` of the coordinate ring. Its stages are affine and of finite type over the
integers, so the hypothesis of the reduction may assume both. The cone is normalized by
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Cone.extend` along the canonical isomorphism of the affine open with the
spectrum of its ring of global sections, so that the vertex is that open subscheme on the nose
and the restricted morphism is a morphism to the vertex without further transport. That
normalization is written as `CategoryTheory.Limits.IsLimit.ofIsoLimit` of
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Cone.extendIso` and its type is left to be read off the term: stating the
type and proving it by `CategoryTheory.Limits.IsLimit.extendIso` instead makes the elaborator
unify two `CategoryTheory.Limits.Cone.extend` terms over the spectrum of a ring of global
sections, which exhausts the default heartbeat budget.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CBY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CBY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GDX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GDX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07PX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07PX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01ZM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01ZM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C5F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C5F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C3I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C3I)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite Stacks

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 07PX] at a stage of the Noetherian approximation of an affine scheme.** The
local rings of the spectrum of the subalgebra of `R` generated by a finite subset are G-rings:
that subalgebra is of finite type over `ℤ`, which is a G-ring, and the local rings of the
spectrum of a G-ring are G-rings, being localizations of it. -/
public theorem isGRing_stalk_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj (R : Type u) [CommRing R]
    (i : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ) (p : (specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).obj i) :
    IsGRing (((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).obj i).presheaf.stalk p) :=
  have := finiteType_adjoinFinset_int R i.unop
  have hA : IsGRing (Algebra.adjoin ℤ ((i.unop : Finset R) : Set R)) :=
    isGRing_basic_examples.{0, u}.2.2.2.2 ℤ _ isGRing_basic_examples.{0, 0}.2.2.1
  StacksDraft.ArtinApproximation.isGRing_stalk_spec _ hA p

end AlgebraicGeometry

namespace Stacks.NodalEtaleLocalStructure

/-- The range of the subscheme of a pulled-back ideal sheaf is the preimage of that of the ideal
sheaf. -/
private theorem range_comap_subschemeι_base {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (I : Y.IdealSheafData)
    (g : X ⟶ Y) :
    Set.range (I.comap g).subschemeι.base = g.base ⁻¹' Set.range I.subschemeι.base := by
  simp only [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι, Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap,
    TopologicalSpace.Closeds.coe_preimage]

/-- **The diagram of Tag 0CBY descends along a cofiltered limit.** Let a scheme `c.pt` be the
limit of a cofiltered inverse system of quasi-compact quasi-separated schemes with affine
transition morphisms, let `f : X ⟶ c.pt` be of finite presentation and at-worst-nodal of
relative dimension one, and let `x` be a point of the relative singular subscheme of `f`. If the
diagram of Tag 0CBY exists for every at-worst-nodal morphism of relative dimension one over a
stage of the system, at every point of its relative singular subscheme, then it exists for `f`
at `x`.

The three inputs are [Stacks, Tag 01ZM] part (1), which produces a model `Y ⟶ D.obj i` of `f`
over a stage; [Stacks, Tag 0C5F], which makes the model at-worst-nodal of relative dimension one
after passing to a later stage; and [Stacks, Tag 0C3I] at index one, which says that the relative
singular subscheme commutes with base change and therefore carries `x` to a point of the relative
singular subscheme of the model. The conclusion for the model gives the conclusion for `f` by
`nonempty_standardNodalDiagram_of_isPullback`. -/
public theorem nonempty_standardNodalDiagram_of_isLimit
    {I : Type u} [Category.{u} I] [IsCofiltered I] (D : I ⥤ Scheme.{u}) (c : Cone D)
    (hc : IsLimit c)
    [∀ {i j : I} (a : i ⟶ j), IsAffineHom (D.map a)]
    [∀ i : I, CompactSpace (D.obj i)] [∀ i : I, QuasiSeparatedSpace (D.obj i)]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ c.pt)
    (hfp : FinitePresentation f) (hf : IsAtWorstNodalOfRelativeDimensionOne f)
    {x : X} (hxsing : x ∈ Set.range (relativeSingularIdeal f).subschemeι.base)
    (H : ∀ (i : I) (Z : Scheme.{u}) (r : Z ⟶ D.obj i) (z : Z),
      IsAtWorstNodalOfRelativeDimensionOne r →
      z ∈ Set.range (relativeSingularIdeal r).subschemeι.base →
      Nonempty (StandardNodalDiagram r z)) :
    Nonempty (StandardNodalDiagram f x) := by
  classical
  -- a model of `f` over a finite stage
  obtain ⟨i, Y, q, g, hqfp, hpb⟩ :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.LimitDescent.exists_isPullback_of_finitePresentation D c hc f hfp
  have : QuasiCompact q := hqfp.2.1
  have : QuasiSeparated q := hqfp.2.2
  have : LocallyOfFinitePresentation q := hqfp.1
  have : CompactSpace Y := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace q
  have : QuasiSeparatedSpace Y := quasiSeparatedSpace_of_quasiSeparated q
  -- the base change of the model to the limit is nodal, in the shape Tag 0C5F consumes
  have hmodel : IsAtWorstNodalOfRelativeDimensionOne (pullback.snd q (c.π.app i)) := by
    have hresp : MorphismProperty.RespectsIso
        (@IsAtWorstNodalOfRelativeDimensionOne.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) :=
      MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderBaseChange.respectsIso
    have hsnd : (hpb.isoIsPullback Y c.pt
          (IsPullback.of_hasPullback q (c.π.app i))).hom ≫ pullback.snd q (c.π.app i) = f :=
      hpb.isoIsPullback_hom_snd _ _ (IsPullback.of_hasPullback q (c.π.app i))
    rw [← MorphismProperty.cancel_left_of_respectsIso
      (@IsAtWorstNodalOfRelativeDimensionOne.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (hpb.isoIsPullback Y c.pt (IsPullback.of_hasPullback q (c.π.app i))).hom
      (pullback.snd q (c.π.app i)), hsnd]
    exact hf
  -- Tag 0C5F: the model is nodal after base change to a later stage
  have : CompactSpace (Over.mk q).left := (inferInstance : CompactSpace Y)
  have : QuasiSeparatedSpace (Over.mk q).left := (inferInstance : QuasiSeparatedSpace Y)
  have : CompactSpace (Over.mk (𝟙 (D.obj i))).left := (inferInstance : CompactSpace (D.obj i))
  have : QuasiSeparatedSpace (Over.mk (𝟙 (D.obj i))).left :=
    (inferInstance : QuasiSeparatedSpace (D.obj i))
  obtain ⟨j, a, hja⟩ :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAtWorstNodalOfRelativeDimensionOne_baseChange_of_limitBaseChange
    D c i (Over.mk q) (Over.mk (𝟙 (D.obj i)))
    (Over.homMk q (by simp)) (by simpa using hqfp.1) hc
    ((isAtWorstNodal_overPullback_iff (c.π.app i) q).mpr hmodel)
  rw [isAtWorstNodal_overPullback_iff] at hja
  -- the model over the later stage, and `f` as its base change
  have hA : IsPullback (pullback.fst q (D.map a)) (pullback.snd q (D.map a)) q (D.map a) :=
    IsPullback.of_hasPullback q (D.map a)
  have hw : g ≫ q = (f ≫ c.π.app j) ≫ D.map a := by
    rw [Category.assoc, c.w a]
    exact hpb.w
  set g' : X ⟶ (pullback q (D.map a) : Scheme.{u}) := hA.lift g (f ≫ c.π.app j) hw with hg'
  have hg'fst : g' ≫ pullback.fst q (D.map a) = g := hA.lift_fst _ _ _
  have hg'snd : g' ≫ pullback.snd q (D.map a) = f ≫ c.π.app j := hA.lift_snd _ _ _
  have hB : IsPullback g' f (pullback.snd q (D.map a)) (c.π.app j) := by
    refine IsPullback.of_right ?_ hg'snd hA
    rw [hg'fst, c.w a]
    exact hpb
  -- the point stays a point of the relative singular subscheme
  have : LocallyOfFinitePresentation (pullback.snd q (D.map a)) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.locallyOfFinitePresentation hja.1.1
  have hcomap : (relativeSingularIdeal (pullback.snd q (D.map a))).comap g' =
      relativeSingularIdeal f :=
    relativeSingularIdeal_comap_of_isPullback g' f (pullback.snd q (D.map a)) (c.π.app j) hB
  rw [← hcomap, range_comap_subschemeι_base] at hxsing
  -- the conclusion at the stage, base changed back to the limit
  obtain ⟨d⟩ := H j (pullback q (D.map a)) (pullback.snd q (D.map a)) (g'.base x) hja hxsing
  exact nonempty_standardNodalDiagram_of_isPullback hB rfl d

/-- **The reduction of Tag 0CBY to a base of finite type over the integers.** Suppose that the
diagram of Tag 0CBY exists whenever the base is affine, Noetherian and of finite type over the
integers — hence locally Noetherian and with G-ring local rings, which are the two standing
hypotheses of [Stacks, Tag 0GDX] — for every at-worst-nodal morphism of relative dimension one
over such a base and every point of its relative singular subscheme. Then it exists for every
at-worst-nodal morphism of relative dimension one over an *arbitrary* base, at every point of its
relative singular subscheme.

This is the opening paragraph of the first proof of Tag 0CBY. The assertion is local on source
and target, so the base is replaced by an affine open `V` containing the image of the point and
the source by an affine open `U` of its inverse image containing the point
(`standardNodalDiagramOfResLE`); `V` is the limit of the spectra of the finitely generated
`ℤ`-subalgebras of `Γ(V, ⊤)` (`AlgebraicGeometry.isLimit_specAdjoinFinsetCone`); and the family
over `V` descends to a stage of that system by `nonempty_standardNodalDiagram_of_isLimit`. -/
public theorem nonempty_standardNodalDiagram_of_finiteTypeOverInt
    (H : ∀ (S' X' : Scheme.{u}) (f' : X' ⟶ S') (x' : X'), IsAffine S' → IsNoetherian S' →
      IsLocallyNoetherian S' → LocallyOfFiniteType (terminal.from S') →
      (∀ s' : S', IsGRing (S'.presheaf.stalk s')) →
      IsAtWorstNodalOfRelativeDimensionOne f' →
      x' ∈ Set.range (relativeSingularIdeal f').subschemeι.base →
      Nonempty (StandardNodalDiagram f' x'))
    {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) (hf : IsAtWorstNodalOfRelativeDimensionOne f)
    {x : X} (hxsing : x ∈ Set.range (relativeSingularIdeal f).subschemeι.base) :
    Nonempty (StandardNodalDiagram f x) := by
  classical
  have : LocallyOfFinitePresentation f := locallyOfFinitePresentation hf.1.1
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType f := inferInstance
  -- an affine open of the base containing the image point, and an affine open of its inverse
  -- image containing the point
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hsV⟩ : ∃ V : S.Opens, IsAffineOpen V ∧ f.base x ∈ V := by
    obtain ⟨_, ⟨V, hV, rfl⟩, hsV, -⟩ := S.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
      (Set.mem_univ (f.base x)) isOpen_univ
    exact ⟨V, hV, hsV⟩
  have : IsAffine V.toScheme := hV
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hxU, e⟩ : ∃ U : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen U ∧ x ∈ U ∧ U ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V := by
    obtain ⟨_, ⟨U, hU, rfl⟩, hxU, e⟩ := X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
      (show x ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ V from hsV) (f ⁻¹ᵁ V).2
    exact ⟨U, hU, hxU, e⟩
  have : IsAffine U.toScheme := hU
  -- the restricted family is at-worst-nodal of relative dimension one
  have hf₁ : IsAtWorstNodalOfRelativeDimensionOne (f.resLE V U e) :=
    IsZariskiLocalAtSource.resLE e hf
  have : LocallyOfFinitePresentation (f.resLE V U e) := locallyOfFinitePresentation hf₁.1.1
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType (f.resLE V U e) := inferInstance
  -- the relative singular subscheme of the restriction is the inverse image of that of `f`
  have hsing : relativeSingularIdeal (f.resLE V U e) =
      (relativeSingularIdeal f).comap U.ι := by
    rw [relativeSingularIdeal_comap_etale f U.ι, ← Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι f e,
      relativeSingularIdeal_comp_etale_base (f.resLE V U e) V.ι]
  have hxsing₁ : (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.toScheme) ∈
      Set.range (relativeSingularIdeal (f.resLE V U e)).subschemeι.base := by
    rw [hsing, range_comap_subschemeι_base]
    exact hxsing
  -- the affine open of the base is the limit of the spectra of the finitely generated
  -- subalgebras of its coordinate ring
  have hc := IsLimit.ofIsoLimit (isLimit_specAdjoinFinsetCone Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤))
    (Cone.extendIso (specAdjoinFinsetCone Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤))
      (V.toScheme.isoSpec.symm : (specAdjoinFinsetCone Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤)).pt ≅ V.toScheme))
  have : ∀ i : (Finset Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤))ᵒᵖ,
      CompactSpace ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤)).obj i) := fun i =>
    have := isAffine_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤) i
    inferInstance
  have : ∀ i : (Finset Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤))ᵒᵖ,
      QuasiSeparatedSpace ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤)).obj i) := fun i =>
    have := isAffine_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤) i
    inferInstance
  have hfp₁ : FinitePresentation (f.resLE V U e) :=
    finitePresentation_of_compactSpace _ inferInstance
  have hstage : ∀ (i : (Finset Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤))ᵒᵖ) (Z : Scheme.{u})
      (r : Z ⟶ (specAdjoinFinsetDiagram Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤)).obj i) (z : Z),
      IsAtWorstNodalOfRelativeDimensionOne r →
      z ∈ Set.range (relativeSingularIdeal r).subschemeι.base →
      Nonempty (StandardNodalDiagram r z) := by
    intro i Z r z hr hz
    exact H _ Z r z (isAffine_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤) i)
      (isNoetherian_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤) i)
      (have := isNoetherian_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤) i; inferInstance)
      (locallyOfFiniteType_terminalFrom_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤) i)
      (isGRing_stalk_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj Γ(V.toScheme, ⊤) i) hr hz
  obtain ⟨d⟩ := nonempty_standardNodalDiagram_of_isLimit _ _ hc
    (f.resLE V U e) hfp₁ hf₁ hxsing₁ hstage
  exact ⟨standardNodalDiagramOfResLE V U e hxU d⟩

end Stacks.NodalEtaleLocalStructure

end
